ml_url":"https://github.com/yanchengnv","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yanchengnv/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yanchengnv/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yanchengnv/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yanchengnv/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yanchengnv/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yanchengnv/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yanchengnv/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yanchengnv/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yanchengnv/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"event":"subscribed","commit_id":null,"commit_url":null,"created_at":"2023-11-26T22:20:06Z","performed_via_github_app":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NVIDIA/NVFlare/issues/comments/1828038815","html_url":"https://github.com/NVIDIA/NVFlare/issues/2166#issuecomment-1828038815","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NVIDIA/NVFlare/issues/2166","id":1828038815,"node_id":"IC_kwDOFy3KIc5s9aif","user":{"login":"yanchengnv","id":58191769,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU4MTkxNzY5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/58191769?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/yanchengnv","html_url":"https://github.com/yanchengnv","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yanchengnv/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yanchengnv/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yanchengnv/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yanchengnv/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yanchengnv/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yanchengnv/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yanchengnv/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yanchengnv/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yanchengnv/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2023-11-27T15:19:06Z","updated_at":"2023-11-27T15:20:18Z","body":"Tal, a few more questions:\r\n- Which server process has this memory problem? There are two server processes: one is the root server process that is started when the system is started; another is for the training job that is started only when the job is deployed.\r\n- What type of aggregator did you use? \r\n- Does this problem happen to all training jobs, or only to this particular job?\r\nThanks.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NVIDIA/NVFlare/issues/comments/1828038815/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"yanchengnv","id":58191769,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU4MTkxNzY5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/58191769?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/yanchengnv","html_url":"https://github.com/yanchengnv","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yanchengnv/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yanchengnv/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yanchengnv/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yanchengnv/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yanchengnv/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yanchengnv/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yanchengnv/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yanchengnv/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yanchengnv/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NVIDIA/NVFlare/issues/comments/1828098734","html_url":"https://github.com/NVIDIA/NVFlare/issues/2166#issuecomment-1828098734","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NVIDIA/NVFlare/issues/2166","id":1828098734,"node_id":"IC_kwDOFy3KIc5s9pKu","user":{"login":"yanchengnv","id":58191769,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU4MTkxNzY5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/58191769?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/yanchengnv","html_url":"https://github.com/yanchengnv","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yanchengnv/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yanchengnv/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yanchengnv/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yanchengnv/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yanchengnv/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yanchengnv/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yanchengnv/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yanchengnv/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yanchengnv/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2023-11-27T15:49:10Z","updated_at":"2023-11-27T15:56:04Z","body":"After staring at the graph for a while, I noticed a few things:\r\n- The training has been going on for over 13 hours. Since each round took a few hours, some aggregation should have happened, but we don't see any memory usage surge in the first 13 hours. This seems to indicate that the training was going fine.\r\n- Then the surge happened. A surge is usually the effect of multiple things added up. If there is a systematic memory leak, the curve should be steadily going up, but not a surge. Is it possible that somehow multiple clients started submitting their model weights to the server at the same time period?\r\n- Another possibility has to do with network speed/stability. Did you see any timeout errors in the client's log? If the client fails to get a task due to timeout, it will send the getTask request again to the server. So if the timeout parameter is too short, it could cause cascading effect: the server keeps trying to send the same task (with model weights) to the clients again and again. This will cause memory surge. \r\n- Did you try to re-run the same job with NVFLARE 2.3.5? If the surge was caused by accidental multiple weight submissions, the chance of that happening again should be low.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NVIDIA/NVFlare/issues/comments/1828098734/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"yanchengnv","id":58191769,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU4MTkxNzY5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/58191769?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/yanchengnv","html_url":"https://github.com/yanchengnv","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yanchengnv/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yanchengnv/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yanchengnv/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yanchengnv/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yanchengnv/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yanchengnv/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yanchengnv/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yanchengnv/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yanchengnv/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NVIDIA/NVFlare/issues/comments/1832385777","html_url":"https://github.com/NVIDIA/NVFlare/issues/2166#issuecomment-1832385777","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NVIDIA/NVFlare/issues/2166","id":1832385777,"node_id":"IC_kwDOFy3KIc5tN_zx","user":{"login":"taleinat","id":532281,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUzMjI4MQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/532281?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/taleinat","html_url":"https://github.com/taleinat","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taleinat/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taleinat/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taleinat/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taleinat/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taleinat/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taleinat/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taleinat/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taleinat/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taleinat/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2023-11-29T17:27:06Z","updated_at":"2023-11-29T17:27:06Z","body":"Hi, I'll provide as many details as I can, but first let me respond quickly to @yanchengnv:\r\n\r\n> The training has been going on for over 13 hours. Since each round took a few hours, some aggregation should have happened, but we don't see any memory usage surge in the first 13 hours. This seems to indicate that the training was going fine.\r\n\r\nIndeed, I agree.\r\n\r\n> Is it possible that somehow multiple clients started submitting their model weights to the server at the same time period?\r\n\r\nThat's not possible, since this training was being run with a single FL client.\r\n\r\n> Did you see any timeout errors in the client's log?\r\n\r\nNo, I did not see anything of the sort.\r\n\r\n> Did you try to re-run the same job with NVFLARE 2.3.5?\r\n\r\nNot yet.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NVIDIA/NVFlare/issues/comments/1832385777/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0